  <desc>Put the products of posted documents on invoices.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Documents to invoice</title>

  <p>The <gui>Documents To Invoice</gui> button of the main window lists every
  posted <link xref="documents_window">document</link> whose products have
  not been invoiced yet.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Select a document.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Import To Invoice</gui>. Its lines are added to the
    customer's draft invoice, at the prices chosen by the button beside it; if
    the customer has an unposted invoice you are asked whether to append them
    to it. The document leaves the list.</p></item>
    <item><p>Open the invoice from <link xref="draft_invoices"/> to check it
    and post it.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>The button beside <gui>Import To Invoice</gui> chooses the prices.
  <gui>Use document prices</gui> brings each line in at the price on the
  document. Click it to switch to <gui>Refresh prices</gui>, which brings each
  line in at the customer's current price for the product, the price a new
  invoice line would get. The choice is remembered. Either way the lines are
  taxed with the customer's <link xref="invoice#tax">tax exemption</link>, if
  they have one.</p>

</page>
